---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Footer from '../components/astro/Footer.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Fast — the performance proof — Wyatt Au"
  ogImage="/og/fast.png"
  description="Every performance claim on this site is enforced by CI budgets: LCP under 1.8s, page weight under 1.2MB, WASM under 650KB. Measured, not asserted."
>
  <main id="main-content" class="pt-32">
    <section class="py-16 px-6 md:px-12 lg:px-24">
      <p class="label mb-6">PROOF PAGE</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl font-bold mb-4" style="font-family: var(--font-display, 'Fraunces', Georgia, serif); letter-spacing: -0.02em; line-height: 1.05;">
        Fast is a budget,<br />not a feeling.
      </h1>
      <p class="text-lg mb-8" style="color: var(--text-secondary); max-width: 720px;">
        Every number on this page is enforced by CI. A regression turns
        the build red before it ships. Measured, not asserted.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="py-8 px-6 md:px-12 lg:px-24 pb-8">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
        <div class="border p-6" style="border-color: var(--border); background: var(--bg-card);">
          <p class="text-4xl font-bold mb-2" style="font-family: var(--font-display, 'Fraunces', Georgia, serif); color: var(--accent);">&lt;1.8s</p>
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold mb-1" style="color: var(--text-primary);">Largest Contentful Paint</p>
          <p class="text-xs" style="color: var(--text-secondary);">Enforced in the home E2E spec. A slow hero fails the build.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="border p-6" style="border-color: var(--border); background: var(--bg-card);">
          <p class="text-4xl font-bold mb-2" style="font-family: var(--font-display, 'Fraunces', Georgia, serif); color: var(--accent);">&lt;1.2MB</p>
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold mb-1" style="color: var(--text-primary);">Total page weight</p>
          <p class="text-xs" style="color: var(--text-secondary);">Transfer size budget, same gate.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="border p-6" style="border-color: var(--border); background: var(--bg-card);">
          <p class="text-4xl font-bold mb-2" style="font-family: var(--font-display, 'Fraunces', Georgia, serif); color: var(--accent);">&lt;650KB</p>
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold mb-1" style="color: var(--text-primary);">WASM engine ceiling</p>
          <p class="text-xs" style="color: var(--text-secondary);">The quant engine ships within a hard CI budget.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="py-8 px-6 md:px-12 lg:px-24 pb-8">
      <p class="section-label">The enforcement stack</p>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <div class="border p-5" style="border-color: var(--border);">
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-2" style="color: var(--text-primary);">Build integrity gate</p>
          <p class="text-xs" style="color: var(--text-secondary);">Stylesheet present per page, WASM ceiling, utility classes, single-flight lock. Existence checks are forbidden — content assertions only.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="border p-5" style="border-color: var(--border);">
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-2" style="color: var(--text-primary);">Lineage gate</p>
          <p class="text-xs" style="color: var(--text-secondary);">Dataset sha256 ↔ study citation ↔ snapshot manifest. Numbers trace to bytes.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="border p-5" style="border-color: var(--border);">
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-2" style="color: var(--text-primary);">Accessibility gate</p>
          <p class="text-xs" style="color: var(--text-secondary);">axe-core scans on five key pages. Zero serious/critical enforced.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="border p-5" style="border-color: var(--border);">
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-2" style="color: var(--text-primary);">Drift + fuzz + audits</p>
          <p class="text-xs" style="color: var(--text-secondary);">Weekly fuzz on quant kernels, vendored-code drift report, monthly supply-chain audit.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="py-8 px-6 md:px-12 lg:px-24 pb-24">
      <p class="section-label">Machine-checked math</p>
      <p class="text-lg mb-4" style="color: var(--text-primary);">
        The concentration bound is a theorem, not a comment.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm mb-6" style="color: var(--text-secondary); max-width: 720px;">
        The Herfindahl-Hirschman index computed by the engine is bounded
        above by 1 for any proper allocation — proved in Lean 4
        (verification/PlychartSpec.lean in the repository, kernel-checked).
        The empirical property tests and weekly fuzz runs enforce the same
        bounds on the compiled artifacts.
      </p>
      <div class="border p-5 font-mono text-xs" style="border-color: var(--border); background: var(--bg-card);">
        theorem hhi_bounded_bp (S : Nat) (ws : List Nat) (hsum : sumBp ws = S) :<br />
        &nbsp;&nbsp;hhiBp ws ≤ S * S<br />
        <span style="color: var(--text-secondary);">-- proof: induction + calc, zero sorry</span>
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm mt-6" style="color: var(--text-secondary);">
        Full contract: <a href="/api/openapi.json" class="hover:underline" style="color: var(--accent);">/api/openapi.json</a>
        · Verified build: <span class="font-mono">/api/metrics</span> for live counters
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
